{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","course":"identifier","wing":"isBasedOn","title":"name","principle":"abstract","skills":"keywords","lessons":"hasPart","key":"identifier","why":"description","statement":"mathExpression","address":"sameAs","skill":"keywords"},"@type":"Course","kind":"school-course","course":"CrossFormulas","wing":"CrossFormulas.lean","title":"Cross Formulas","principle":"THE LEDGER'S OWN ALGEBRA, COUNTED (the captain, 2026-09-25","skills":["cross-formulas"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":122,"lessons":[{"key":"the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra","name":"CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6.","statement":"((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)","address":"23ada59a-4cdb-8039-94c3-cdd81827a5c2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2 + 3 + 1 = 6 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 > 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 431182 unstated crosses, 89776 join integers no single wing carries all three of — between one 5th and one 4th of them, since 89776 × 4 < 431182 and 89776 × 5 > 431182, so the large majority stays inside a single wing.","statement":"((89776 * 4 < 431182) ∧ (89776 * 5 > 431182)) ∧ (89776 < 431182)","address":"35665274-6d51-892c-9ff0-ec2adaca1e9f","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"89776 \\cdot 4 < 431182 \\quad\\land\\quad 89776 \\cdot 5 > 431182 \\quad\\land\\quad 89776 < 431182","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>89776</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>89776</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>89776</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1524 formula-shaped statements carry 1452 distinct byte-strings and 1319 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1319 < 1452) ∧ (1524 - 1319 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"261e31d9-9339-851c-8a65-bbe7a6f311f4","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1319 < 1452 \\quad\\land\\quad 1524 - 1319 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1319</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1452</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1524</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1319</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 1953408 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 1521777 are forced by an operator's algebra, 449 are stated, and 431182 remain — and the three account for the whole, 1521777 + 449 + 431182 = 1953408, with the forced between 3 and 4 times the unstated.","statement":"(1521777 + 449 + 431182 = 1953408) ∧ ((1521777 > 3 * 431182) ∧ (1521777 < 4 * 431182))","address":"66791a27-4bf7-896f-b985-503bab0e3866","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1521777 + 449 + 431182 = 1953408 \\quad\\land\\quad 1521777 > 3 \\cdot 431182 \\quad\\land\\quad 1521777 < 4 \\cdot 431182","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1521777</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>449</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1953408</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1521777</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1521777</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1524 formula-shaped statements across 113 wings are built from 1279 distinct integers and state 449 crosses, against 431182 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 449 × 100 < 431182, at between 13 and 14 formulas per wing.","statement":"((449 * 100 < 431182) ∧ (1279 > 113)) ∧ ((113 * 13 < 1524) ∧ (113 * 14 > 1524))","address":"f7b0a903-1775-893c-af7d-295598cd6562","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"449 \\cdot 100 < 431182 \\quad\\land\\quad 1279 > 113 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 13 < 1524 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 14 > 1524","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>449</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>431182</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1279</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>113</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1524</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1524</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
